    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 7 with a high-upside lineup anchored by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98), who registers our highest score of the day. Despite a 36% rain risk, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a mandatory start due to a favorable matchup against Lowder and significant wind assistance, which pushes his efficiency score well into the strong territory. **Junior Caminero** (69.27) and **Trea Turner** (68.62) follow closely behind; **Junior Caminero** benefits from a strong park factor and a solid SP skill advantage against Bennett, while **Trea Turner** remains a centerpiece of our offensive strategy. With J.T. Ginn on the mound, we are banking on **Trea Turner** leveraging his elite sprint speed against a pitcher whose delivery profile provides a 4% efficiency boost for potential stolen bases\u2014our most critical category.\n\nRounding out the lineup, **Kyle Schwarber** (62.66) and **Carson Benge** (60.00) provide the necessary depth to maintain our production floor. While **Carson Benge** faces a difficult L/L platoon disadvantage against Quintana, the high park factor and Quintana's elevated xERA mitigate that risk enough to keep him active. **Caleb Durbin** (41.71) lands on the lower end of our starting threshold; while his raw projections are modest, his 100% stolen base opportunity against Jax makes him too valuable to bench given the scarcity of speed in our current roster construct. Our bench remains stagnant today due to scheduled off-days for **Yordan Alvarez**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Kazuma Okamoto**, alongside **Christian Yelich** who continues his recovery on the IL. With the rest of our depth\u2014including **Colt Keith**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Zac Veen**, **Luke Raley**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**\u2014holding no active games today, we are fully committed to the current active roster to navigate this mid-week slate.",
